{"id": 28, "ts": 1780444440.907913, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s support for Candidate\u202fC and James\u2019s clarification that we have no concrete evidence of Candidate\u202fB\u2019s adaptability or openness to feedback. That gap is significant because adaptability and feedback orientation are essential for long\u2011distance crew dynamics. While Candidate\u202fB is very conscientious, handles stress well, and assesses weather expertly, the notes also flag that they are sometimes pretentious and adopt the wrong tone when communicating. Those traits could undermine crew cooperation and professional communication, especially without proof they can adjust their style.\nCandidate\u202fC, on the other hand, makes correct decisions quickly, has excellent attention skills, and consistently puts concern for others above everything\u2014behaviors that directly support calm, safe decision\u2011making and crew teamwork. Although C is described as egocentric and not very willing to pursue further education, the egocentric label seems at odds with their strong other\u2011oriented concern, and the lack of willingness to continue education is less critical for the immediate operational demands than the communication tone issues we see with B.\nGiven the missing adaptability evidence for B and the stronger collaborative indicators for C, I am shifting my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**."}
